rhodep-aireplay-settle
======================

Wrapper around /usr/sbin/aireplay-ng that pre-settles the WCN3990 monitor
vdev before exec'ing the real binary. Works around a firmware bug where
the mgmt-forwarder goes silent after any chanctx transition.

See kernel/ath10k-rhodep-port/docs/5ghz-mgmt-forwarder-bug.md for the
full analysis.

Layout
------
    /usr/local/sbin/aireplay-ng-settle   the wrapper shell script
    /usr/sbin/aireplay-ng                symlink -> the wrapper
    /usr/sbin/aireplay-ng.real           the original aircrack-ng binary

On any invocation:
  1. wrapper parses -i, -c/--channel and positional iface arg
  2. falls back to `iw dev wlan0mon info` to read current channel
  3. iw set channel to an adjacent channel (forces fw chanctx transition)
  4. sleep 1
  5. iw set channel back to target
  6. sleep 1
  7. exec /usr/sbin/aireplay-ng.real with original argv
Total overhead: ~2 seconds per invocation.

Bypass
------
For debugging or one-off use of the real binary:
    sudo /usr/sbin/aireplay-ng.real ...

Uninstall
---------
    sudo dpkg -r rhodep-aireplay-settle
The prerm removes the symlink and restores the original binary.

Why not fix the driver
----------------------
Two attempts crashed the firmware at cmnos_thread.c:4005. WMI cmd needed
(wmi_vdev_param_rx_filter_promisc) is UNSUPPORTED in mainline ath10k
WMI-TLV table. Fw-level architectural limitation of WCN3990.
